  "answer": "### Short Answer\nIf you have missed the deadline for filing your annual income tax return, you may face penalties and interest on the unpaid tax. It is advisable to file your return as soon as possible to minimize these penalties.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is Section 51 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which outlines the requirements for filing income tax returns and the consequences of failing to do so.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nPractically, if you have missed the deadline, you should file your return immediately to avoid further penalties. The longer you wait, the more interest and penalties may accrue. Additionally, if you owe taxes, paying them promptly can help reduce the financial impact of late fees. It is also advisable to keep records of your filing and payment to address any future inquiries from the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
